   "text": "The molecule is a PROTAC-type degrader. It joins an entrectinib-like indazole benzamide to a VHL ligand (hydroxyproline / tert-leucine / 4-methylthiazolylbenzylamine) through a piperazine and a decanedioyl (sebacoyl) linker.\n\n**Left-hand ligand**\n- The 3,5-difluorobenzyl group sits on C5 of a 1H-indazole.\n- The indazole C3 carries an NH\u2013C(=O) amide to a benzene ring.\n- On that benzene ring, ortho to the amide, is an NH-(tetrahydropyran-4-yl) group.\n- Para to the amide is a piperazine nitrogen.\n\n**Linker**\n- The other piperazine nitrogen is acylated by a decanedioyl chain: C(=O), eight CH2, C(=O).\n- The chain atoms from carbonyl to carbonyl total ten.\n\n**VHL ligand**\n- The far carbonyl forms an amide with the NH of tert-leucine, which is drawn with a hashed bond.\n- The tert-leucine carbonyl is attached to the nitrogen of a 4-hydroxypyrrolidine-2-carboxamide.\n- The pyrrolidine C2 carries a hashed bond and C4 the wedged OH. I assigned the stereodescriptors by comparison with the standard VHL ligand (2S,4R, tert-leucine S), checking the permutation parity of each centre.\n- The carboxamide nitrogen bears a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzyl group.\n\nSMILES: O=C(c1ccc(cc1NC1CCOCC1)N1CCN(CC1)C(=O)CCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)NCc1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C)Nc1n[nH]c2ccc(Cc3cc(F)cc(F)c3)cc12"
  }
